Your data will be stored separately:

text
/home/rajesh/
│
├── gps_raw/
│   ├── ublox7_20261030_220000.txt
│   └── ublox7_20261030_230000.txt
│
└── livox_bags/
    ├── mid360s_20261030_220000.bag
    └── mid360s_20261030_230000.bag

Important notes for data collection
GPS: Keep the antenna outdoors with a clear view of the sky.
LiDAR: Maintain the Ethernet connection throughout recording.
IMU: Verify that messages are continuously arriving.
Storage: Your earlier 56.7-second LiDAR + IMU recording occupied approximately 286 MB. Make sure you have sufficient disk space.
Synchronization: These are separate recordings, so their timestamps are not automatically synchronized. For later sensor fusion, we'll need to establish a common time reference.
One recommendation

For your eventual LiDAR–IMU–GPS SLAM dataset, I recommend eventually recording all three sensors in one ROS bag, while also preserving the original raw GPS NMEA text file as a backup.

That gives you both ROS-compatible data and the original GPS measurements.
